---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy (Client-Side & AdSense Disclosures) | Taprico"
  description="Taprico Privacy Policy covering client-side tool execution, localStorage preferences, Google AdSense cookies, GDPR, and California CCPA/CPRA rights."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
    <header class="space-y-2 border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 pb-6">
      <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-600 dark:text-indigo-400">
        Privacy Policy
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Privacy Policy for {SITE.domain}</h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Effective Date: November 17, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">1. Client-Side Tool Processing (Zero Payload Storage)</h2>
      <p>
        Every developer and freelance utility on {SITE.name} ({SITE.url})—including JSON/YAML formatting, JWT decoding and HMAC verification, Cron parsing, Regex testing, Base64 conversion, UUID generation, SQL formatting, Diff comparison, Invoice PDF generation, and financial calculators—executes locally inside your web browser. Data you paste into tool inputs is never transmitted to, stored on, or logged by {SITE.name} servers.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">2. Local Browser Storage</h2>
      <p>
        We use your browser’s <code class="font-mono text-indigo-500">localStorage</code> strictly to remember optional user preferences, such as your Dark/Light theme choice and saved business defaults inside the Invoice Generator. You can clear this data at any time through your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">3. Advertising, Cookies &amp; Google AdSense</h2>
      <p>
        To keep {SITE.name} free without paywalls, we may display advertisements served by Google AdSense and its certified ad-technology partners. Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies or similar identifiers to serve ads based on a visitor’s prior visits to {SITE.domain} or other websites across the internet.
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
        <li>
          Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visits to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.
        </li>
        <li>
          You may opt out of personalized advertising anytime by visiting{' '}
          <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-indigo-500 hover:underline">
            Google Ads Settings
          </a>{' '}
          or via{' '}
          <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="text-indigo-500 hover:underline">
            aboutads.info
          </a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">4. US State Privacy Rights (CCPA / CPRA) &amp; GDPR</h2>
      <p>
        Residents of California, Virginia, Colorado, Texas, and the European Economic Area have the right to request disclosure regarding cookie usage, restrict personalized advertising cookies via browser or Google consent controls, and contact us with privacy questions at{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`} class="font-mono text-indigo-500 hover:underline">{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        Because we do not operate user accounts or collect personal databases of tool payloads, we do not sell personal input data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-2">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5. Static Hosting &amp; Server Logs</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.domain} is served via static edge hosting/CDN infrastructure, which may temporarily process standard HTTP access metadata (such as IP address, user-agent, and request timestamp) strictly for DDoS mitigation, TLS termination, and reliability.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
